# Docker does NOT read .gitignore. Everything excluded there has to be repeated
# here or it lands in the build context and then in an image layer — which is
# public, immutable, and not deletable after the fact.
#
# The hard requirement this file exists to enforce: no local portfolio data and
# no secrets reach the cloud image. Dockerfile also asserts on this (see the
# guard stage) rather than trusting these patterns to stay correct.

# ── Real portfolio data ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# db/ holds wealthcompass.db plus four backups. None of it belongs in an image.
#
# The `**/` prefixes are load-bearing, not decoration. .dockerignore matches with
# Go's filepath.Match, where `*` never crosses a `/` — so a bare `*.db` matches
# only at the context root and silently misses nested ones. Running the app from
# the wrong directory has already left empty stray databases at
# backend/wealthcompass.db and backend/app/db/wealthcompass.db; those happened to
# be 0 bytes, but the pattern that let them through would pass a real one too.
# (git's `*.db` DOES match at any depth, which is why .gitignore looks correct
# and this file needs to be written differently.)
# Directory patterns are ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading slash. A bare `db/` (or
# worse, `**/db/`) also matches backend/app/db/ — which is source code, not data,
# and excluding it breaks the image with `No module named 'backend.app.db'`.
# The three data directories all live at the repo root; the only `db` elsewhere
# holds schema.py.
/db/
/data/

# File patterns stay recursive: stray databases turn up outside /db/ when the app
# is run from the wrong directory (backend/wealthcompass.db and
# backend/app/db/wealthcompass.db both exist). These exclude the files while
# leaving their directories — and therefore schema.py — in place.
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# The personal ticker allowlist. Discloses the real holdings on its own, with
# no database attached. process.py ignores it in demo mode, but the safest
# version of that is for the file to not exist in the image.
/config/

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.env
.gemini/
GoogleAIStudio/

# ── Build noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Not a registered router, and its `import vertexai` would drag in
# google-cloud-aiplatform. Excluded so the image cannot grow a dependency on it.
backend/app/api/archive/

# ── Local-only tooling and notes ─────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
scripts/
server.sh
test_manual_parser.sh
*.md
!README.md
docs/
backend/tests/
last_commit_hash.txt
